  CardStory: "Hm, that means I said something wrong. She asks what Spades2 is talking
    about. That didn\u2019t happen, did it? The heating worked. Spades2 agrees. Ah,
    you\u2019re right, of course. I must be misremembering. Spades2 blinks and frowns.
    This winter is not as bad as the last one. But was the last one truly bad? Spades2
    doesn\u2019t think so, and everyone else seems to have forgotten.\r\n\r\nStill,
    the barracks are warm enough, unlike the outer walls. Most bunks are occupied,
    which makes sense. Each soldier has a bunk. But there is an empty one next to
    mine. Why is it empty? Bunks should have soldiers in them. I remember the soldier
    who used to be there. \r\n\r\nThe bunk is there, but when Spades2 asks the others
    about him, no one knows what I am talking about. Spades2 is told it was never
    occupied. He thinks they are right, he knows there was never a soldier there.
    Why did I think there was? Because there must have been. All bunks have a soldier.
    I just can\u2019t remember what his face looked like.\r\n\r\nSpades2 sleeps."
